{"chunk_id": "aba40849fba4", "text": "Yudhishthira instructs Sanjaya to deliver a carefully balanced message to the Kuru court. While acknowledging Dhritarashtra\u2019s past support, he insists that the Pandavas deserve their rightful share of the kingdom. Yudhishthira emphasizes restraint: despite grave insults\u2014especially Draupadi\u2019s humiliation and their exile\u2014the Pandavas have endured in order to avoid the destruction of the Kuru family. He proposes peace on remarkably modest terms, asking even for just five villages to avert war. Sanjaya then travels to Hastinapura and reports to Dhritarashtra, describing Yudhishthira as virtuous, restrained, and guided by righteousness rather than greed. He warns the blind king that destiny and the consequences of his own wrongful choices threaten disaster, subtly urging him to reconsider before conflict becomes inevitable.\nYudhishthira sends Sanjaya to urge peace, asking Dhritarashtra and Duryodhana for reconciliation and even five villages to avoid war.\nThemes: peace diplomacy, just kingship, forgiveness of insults, destiny vs effort, family reconciliation", "vector": [-0.004371929913759232, -0.018468966707587242, -0.011942996643483639, 0.020068535581231117, 0.004869274795055389, 0.03470660373568535, -0.019813142716884613, -0.00396867748349905, -0.005279248114675283, -0.022676236927509308, 0.016331728547811508, 0.0030596789438277483, 0.013979421928524971, 0.02154712937772274, -0.011842183768749237, 0.0041434201411902905, 0.053444407880306244, -0.009059741161763668, 0.028308330103754997, -0.014974111691117287, -0.012366412207484245, -0.020014768466353416, -0.002938703168183565, 0.009342017583549023, -0.030163291841745377, 0.03473348915576935, 0.02273000217974186, -0.012467225082218647, -0.01297801174223423, -0.017272651195526123, -0.006562935654073954, 0.006878816522657871, 0.013146033510565758, 0.0011501099215820432, -0.030566545203328133, 0.011848904192447662, -0.006727597210556269, -0.013858446851372719, 0.0